error[E0706]: `[3]F32` can't stand in for the C type `lib_Pair`
 --> tests/ui/cimport_errors/main.wid:1:68
  |
1 | cimport "lib.h", as: :lib, strip_prefix: "lib_", types: {lib_Pair: [3]F32, lib_Pare: [2]F32}
  |                                                                    ^^^^^^ `[3]F32` is 12 bytes, aligned to 4
  |                                                          -------- `lib_Pair` is 8 bytes, aligned to 4
  = note: a mapped type is copied byte for byte, so both must have the same size and alignment
help: map `lib_Pair` to a Wid type with the same fields, or remove it from `types:`
  = see `wid explain E0706`

error[E0703]: `lib_Pare` is not a struct or union in `lib.h`
 --> tests/ui/cimport_errors/main.wid:1:76
  |
1 | cimport "lib.h", as: :lib, strip_prefix: "lib_", types: {lib_Pair: [3]F32, lib_Pare: [2]F32}
  |                                                                            ^^^^^^^^ `types:` maps C records to Wid types
help: did you mean `lib_Pair`?
  | cimport "lib.h", as: :lib, strip_prefix: "lib_", types: {lib_Pair: [3]F32, lib_Pair: [2]F32}
  = see `wid explain E0703`

error[E0701]: header `missing.h` not found
