error[E0703]: `cimport` has no option `strip:`
 --> tests/ui/cimport_errors/main.wid:3:30
  |
3 | cimport "lib.h", as: :again, strip: "lib_", rename: :camel
  |                              ^^^^^ unknown option
  = note: options: as, strip_prefix, rename, names, types, define, implement, link, pkg_config, include_dirs
  = see `wid explain E0703`

error[E0703]: `rename:` takes `:snake_case` (the default) or `:keep`
 --> tests/ui/cimport_errors/main.wid:3:53
  |
3 | cimport "lib.h", as: :again, strip: "lib_", rename: :camel
  |                                                     ^^^^^^ not accepted here
  = note: `:snake_case` turns `InitWindow` into `init_window`; `:keep` only lowercases the first letter of functions
  = see `wid explain E0703`

error[E0708]: only `@[extern]` methods take C variadic arguments
 --> tests/ui/cimport_errors/main.wid:5:25
  |
5 | def local(fmt: CString, ...)
  |                         ^^^ `...` passes extra arguments the C way, which only C code can read
help: take the extra values as a slice with a `*rest: T` parameter instead
  = see `wid explain E0708`

error[E0705]: `LIB_TWICE` from `lib.h` was not imported
 --> tests/ui/cimport_errors/main.wid:9:12
  |
9 |   puts lib.TWICE(2)
  |            ^^^^^ `LIB_TWICE` is a function-like macro
  = note: C declares it at lib.h:4
help: write a small C function in a `.c` file of the package that calls the macro, and declare it with `@[extern]`
  = see `wid explain E0705`

error[E0704]: `log` is ambiguous: `lib_Log` and `lib_log` both become `log` in Wid
  --> tests/ui/cimport_errors/main.wid:10:7
   |
10 |   lib.log(1.0)
   |       ^^^ cimport left both out
   = note: cimport turns C names into Wid names with fixed rules, and these end up the same
help: give the others their own names, so `log` means `lib_Log`
   | cimport "lib.h", as: :lib, strip_prefix: "lib_", types: {lib_Pair: [3]F32, lib_Pare: [2]F32}, names: {lib_log: :log_2}
   = see `wid explain E0704`

error[E0707]: `Handle` is opaque, so it can only be used through a pointer
  --> tests/ui/cimport_errors/main.wid:11:11
   |
11 |   handle: lib.Handle
   |           ^^^^^^^^^^ this needs a whole `Handle`
   = note: C hides the fields and size of an opaque struct; only the library that defines it can create one
help: point at it instead
   |   handle: ^lib.Handle
   = see `wid explain E0707`

error[E0708]: `String` can't be passed through C's `...`
  --> tests/ui/cimport_errors/main.wid:12:21
   |
12 |   lib.print("%s\n", "text".to_s)
   |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^ this is `String`
   = note: C variadic arguments take numbers, pointers, C strings and C structs
help: pass a C string
   |   lib.print("%s\n", "text".to_s.to_cstr)
   = see `wid explain E0708`

